I think you meant: {ca'e ro da poi valsi zo'u la'e da sidbo},
for every word, its referent is an idea.

I think {la'e ro valsi} does not say "for every word, its referent",
but rather "the (common) referent of every word". At least this is
how other members of LAhE work. {lu'o ro valsi} is "the (common)
mass containing every word", and not "for every word, that word
considered as a mass".

